   "where": "Wolford Dragons at Stanton City Conductors, week 20",
   "text": "Lakshmi Coldcombe (DL, Dragons) hit Nayeli Brokenrope (WR, Conductors) in a defenseless position with 8:04 left in the first quarter and was flagged for unnecessary roughness. Brokenrope stayed in the game (he scored a touchdown later in the second quarter).\n\nWHAT HAPPENED: Brokenrope was reaching up for a pass over the middle when Coldcombe drove a forearm into his head and neck area, before the ball had arrived. It was one hit, with no words and no contact after the whistle, and he did not stand over the player.\n\nSEVERITY: moderate. The league's film review found that the target was the head and neck, which is a protected area for a receiver who has not yet caught the ball, and that Coldcombe had time to pull up. No injury, no ejection, no earlier cases for Coldcombe in the last three seasons. His agent, Dalia Okonkwo-Pryce, says the player will cooperate with the review.",
